From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bitpony <bitpony@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockbase: sdhci-of-kendryte force PIO (disable ADMA+SDMA)
 diagnostic

Rockbase silent hard-lockup diagnostic. Both the SD card and the RTL8189FS
SDIO WiFi on the 1G and 2G boards are driven by this same kendryte SDHCI
controller, and both controllers are dma-noncoherent and use ADMA. Field
reports show 1G and 2G freeze at a similar, random rate with no panic/oops
(single-core, no hardlockup detector), which is consistent with a shared
DMA cache-coherency race on the dma-noncoherent ADMA path.

Force PIO by disabling both ADMA and SDMA. SDHCI core clears
SDHCI_USE_SDMA on SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_DMA and SDHCI_USE_ADMA on
SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_ADMA, leaving PIO only. If the freeze disappears on
both boards under PIO, the root cause is the DMA/cache-coherency path; if
it persists, DMA coherency is ruled out.

DEBUG ONLY. PIO is slow and CPU-heavy on this single core; this patch must
be reverted for production images.

Signed-off-by: bitpony <bitpony@example.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-kendryte.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-kendryte.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-kendryte.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-kendryte.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-kendryte.c
@@ -293,9 +293,18 @@ static const struct sdhci_ops sdhci_dwcmshc_kendryte_ops = {
 	.voltage_switch = dwcmshc_phy_1_8v_init,
 };
 
 static const struct sdhci_pltfm_data sdhci_dwcmshc_kendryte_pdata = {
 	.ops = &sdhci_dwcmshc_kendryte_ops,
-	.quirks = SDHCI_QUIRK_CAP_CLOCK_BASE_BROKEN,
+	/*
+	 * rockbase freeze diagnostic (DEBUG ONLY, revert for production):
+	 * force PIO by disabling both ADMA and SDMA so the dma-noncoherent
+	 * ADMA path (shared by SD card and RTL8189FS SDIO on 1G/2G) is
+	 * removed. Used to test whether the random silent hard-lockup is a
+	 * DMA cache-coherency race. PIO is slow and CPU-heavy on this single
+	 * core.
+	 */
+	.quirks = SDHCI_QUIRK_CAP_CLOCK_BASE_BROKEN |
+		  SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_ADMA | SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_DMA,
 };
 
 static unsigned int slot_index;
